{{/*
The guarded family: one line of method wiring over the engine primitive
that owns the semantics. What "reports a cancelled context" means, and
what the failure says, lives in engine/suite and is not restated here.

One define rather than one per guard. The arms differ in the primitive's
NAME, which is data the body carries, and three defines matching byte
for byte apart from one literal are three places to fix the day the
closure changes shape.
*/}}
{{- define "suite.body.guarded-call" -}}
{{- $call := suite_callExpr .Recv .Body.Call -}}
{{ renderExpr (external .Vocab .Guard) }}(tb, {{ .Check }}, func(ctx {{ renderExpr (external "context" "Context") }}) error {
{{- if .ErrBind }}
	{{ .ErrBind }} {{ $call }}
	return err
{{- else }}
	return {{ $call }}
{{- end }}
})
{{- end -}}
